{"id": "86149", "name": "פתיחת סוגריים עם שורשים – (√c − a)(√c + b) (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "none", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>Expand the following:</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">\\({{CT:0}} =\\) [[input:ans]]</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans]]</div><p class=\"input-hint input-hint-root\" dir=\"ltr\" style=\"font-size:0.88em;color:#555;margin:6px 0 0;text-align:left\">How to enter: a square root as <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(...)</code>, e.g. <code dir=\"ltr\">sqrt(5*x)</code>. Other roots as a power, with brackets around the exponent: \\(\\sqrt[3]{x+1}\\) is entered as <code dir=\"ltr\">(x+1)^(1/3)</code>.</p></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Multiply out the brackets</b><br>When multiplying out brackets involving surds the method is very much the same. Just remember that<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ \\sqrt{x}\\sqrt{x}=x^{\\frac{1}{2}}\\times x^{\\frac{1}{2}} = x^{\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}}=x. \\]</p>In this example (multiply each term of the first bracket by each term of the second, then collect the terms with the surd):<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:1}} = {{CT:2}}-{{CT:3}}\\sqrt{{CT:2}}+{{CT:4}}\\sqrt{{CT:2}}-{{CT:5}} = {{CT:6}}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<p><span class=\"correct\">Correct answer, well done.</span></p>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<p><span class=\"partially\">Your answer is partially correct.</span></p>", "prtincorrect": "<p><span class=\"incorrect\">Incorrect answer.</span></p>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "expand", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "prt1", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "EqualComAss", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-0-T ", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "1-0-F ", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans", "tans": "ta", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-T ", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Your answer is algebraically equivalent to the correct answer but you need to multiply out the brackets and leave the answer as a number in the form \\(a+\\sqrt{b}\\). </div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "1-1-F ", "feedback": ""}}]}], "qvnames": ["a", "b", "c", "ta"], "nvariants": 50}